; ONE VARIABLE: `layout_direction = 3` (RTL) on the lower TabBar.
;
; Under RTL a TabBar draws every tab at `size.width - ofs_cache - size_cache`
; (tab_bar.cpp:552,1929) and then flows that tab's own icon, title and close
; icon BACK from `size_cache - the style's LEFT margin` (:660,668,676,721) —
; the left margin measured off the right edge, which is why `tab_selected` is
; overridden here with a deliberately lopsided 24/6 pair. The inline
; GradientTexture2D on the first tab is asymmetric along X, so a mirrored icon
; cannot be mistaken for an unmirrored one, and `tab_close_display_policy = 2`
; keeps a close icon on every tab as the trailing element of that flow. Both
; bars anchor to the same symmetric rect, so the node's OWN rect is
; mirror-invariant and only the inside of the strip can move.
;
; `unit-tab-bar-rtl-scroll` moves the scroll arrows under the same property
; and draws no icon or close button; every other TabBar scene is LTR.

[gd_scene load_steps=4 format=3]

[sub_resource type="StyleBoxFlat" id="StyleBoxFlat_selected"]
